ll FAILING at HEAD. The fix belongs in the battery harness's evidence path (write under a gitignored scratch root or a tracked evidence root with an INDEX), not only in .gitignore.\n\nRECURRENCE CONFIRMED A THIRD TIME 2026-11-24T22:35Z (COS card manager, append-only). Residue under .coding-hermes/evidence/ is now THREE untracked battery dirs, not two: qa-20261122T202851Z (168K), qa-20261123T144739Z (148K), and NEW qa-20261124T210609Z (created 2026-11-24T16:07-05 during the lore-foreman-2026-11-24-20-42-52 / lore-ops battery, dir mtime 2026-11-24 16:07), 464K total. git status --porcelain at origin/main 247007c still reports \"?? .coding-hermes/evidence/\", and .gitignore carries no entry for the path (grep -n 'coding-hermes/evidence' .gitignore returns nothing).\n\nDirection this narrows for the fixer: the generator is running once per battery run, so a .gitignore entry alone leaves the release dry-run clean-tree precheck dependent on a rule a future harness edit can drop, while the harness's evidence path keeps minting 148-168K per run. The fix belongs in the battery harness evidence path (write under ~/.hermes/qa, or a path already ignored), with .gitignore as belt-and-braces only.\n\nDISCLOSURES: (a) the harness half lives OUTSIDE any git repo — deployed at ~/.hermes/scripts/bunker-qa.sh (the versioned backup trail is its history; the coding-hermes-tools mirror is a periodic-sync copy deliberately left untouched); the graded tips therefore carry the belt layer + evidence artifact, and the harness change is bound by sha256 035b26fe... in SHA256SUMS.txt — a later read proves the deployed copy still carries the fix. (b) release.sh full-dry-run cannot exit 0 at any tip until the NEXT version is stamped because v0.3.0 tag already exists — the row's demanded surface is the clean-tree precheck, which prints ok and is no longer a refusal reason at any tip. (c) the graded tip f360eb8 sits one board-commit behind closeout tip by design (lore close order: update uncommitted