 {"id":"LORE-20261012","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"bug","title":"[P2] Armed weekly lore schedules silently missed their first Monday run (2026-11-23): timer says triggered, service never ran, no shipped way to notice","reasoning":"Dogfood run 18 at HEAD 23f800b. Both lore user timers are enabled+active on this host (armed 2026-11-20 per SUP-DEPS-LORE-20261121). This mornings 07:30 lore-validate and 07:45 lore-dep-drift schedules appended NOTHING: ~/.local/share/lore/dep-drift.log mtime 2026-11-20 22:52 (foreman manual run), weekly-validate.log mtime 2026-11-16 07:30. The dep-drift timer records LastTriggerUSec=Mon 2026-11-23 07:56:59 Result=success while the bound service has ZERO journal entries ever (journalctl --user -u = no entries any date). Host context same window: earlyoom SIGKILL storm 07:47:08 (mem avail 1.57%, swap 0.01%; hermes/bunker/gitlab-runner killed), journald Forwarding missed 226 messages 08:04:18, user manager restarted twice 08:22:33/40 (timers stopped+started under new pids). Net: a missed scheduled run is invisible in every surface lore ships; the timer state actively misleads; the report-log mtime is the only honest signal and deploy/systemd/README.md does not document checking it. The script itself works (manual run: rc 0, 1.45s, honest 4-of-34 report).","acceptance_criteria":"1) deploy/systemd/README.md documents a post-Monday verification check for each armed timer (report-log mtime or equivalent) with the exact paths. 2) A missed run is DETECTABLE: either dep-drift.sh/validate path appends a dated heartbeat line even on the no-op path, or the units ship an OnFailure/monitor that surfaces a missed service start. 3) The README caveat from run 18 (timer state can say triggered while the service never ran) is present in the systemd arming section. Evidence: docs/qa/evidence/run18/INDEX.md timer-miss section.","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-23T14:51:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-23T22:17:43+00:00","created_by":null,"source":null,"capability_tags":["docs","ops"],"detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"48eb7db7443f90ad118077fdfa74968b2dc7d7a7f2136df2de0ba4bb9b2a005f","evidence":[{"run_id":"7425a512","ts":"2026-11-23T22:17:43+00:00"}]},"branch":"main","worktree":null,"commit_hash":"5d9eec8dbff402b82d588d7630fe1477e53fc0c8","guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"completed_at":"2026-11-23T15:32:00+00:00","worker_status":"complete","foreman_note":"Tick lore-foreman-2026-11-23-15-26-24: serial worker (glm-5.3-flash@ollama-cloud). Commit 1f24826e810d8649d31f10b3798f8e02c72ca22b: dep-drift.sh appends dated heartbeat line even on no-op path (live-verified: heartbeat 2026-11-23T10:30:16-0500 rc=0); OnFailure wired via companion unit lore-dep-drift-failure.service + dep-drift-failure-notice.sh helper (avoids %-specifier mangling); deploy/systemd/README.md documents post-Monday mtime verification check per timer with exact paths + run-18 caveat citing docs/qa/evidence/run18/INDEX.md. Gates on committed tree: 586 pytest passed, dep_drift_test 2 passed, ruff check+format clean, count guard PASS canonical=586 class-count=13. Weekly-validate unit is host-local (not in deploy/systemd/) so its fix is the documented mtime check, stated honestly. (row commit_hash repointed to graded tip 5d9eec8dbff402b82d588d7630fe1477e53fc0c8; product/work commit remains 1f24826e810d.)\n\nCOS card manager 2026-11-23T22:2xZ: close VERIFIED, evidence now shipped. gitreins tier-2 judge run 7425a512 at .gitreins/history/2026-11-23/7425a512/verdict.json carries task_id=LORE-20261012, passed=true, pass_class=judged, commit=5d9eec8, evaluated_at=2026-11-23T15:34:37Z; it was UNTRACKED when the row closed and is committed by this pass so origin/main readers and worktree workers can resolve it. Row carried evidence:null before this binding. CITATION DRIFT, recorded not repaired: the close commit 07a42fa message names verdict id aa084b7e, which resolves to no artifact anywhere in the tree or history (grep across