 {"id":"LORE-20261013","status":"pending","priority":"P4","type":"bug","title":"[P4] docs/ABSORB-TRIGGER.md never names the adapter method: a verbatim consumer calls .parse() and gets AttributeError (real method is .read())","reasoning":"Dogfood run 18: the consumer was written exactly from docs/ABSORB-TRIGGER.md, which says AugerDecisionTableAdapter(path) parses Augers deterministic Markdown export but shows no method call (the code sample only demonstrates BoardEventWatcher.consume()). First attempt called .parse() -> AttributeError: AugerDecisionTableAdapter object has no attribute parse (lore/trigger.py:219 defines read()). One added sentence or a two-line example with a.read() removes the only dead end in an otherwise working doc page. Board-watcher half of the page is complete and was driven successfully over the repo board (117 blocks -> 4 proposals, no replay on restart).","acceptance_criteria":"docs/ABSORB-TRIGGER.md shows or names the adapter call (AugerDecisionTableAdapter(...).read()); a consumer following only that page runs it with no source dive. Evidence: docs/qa/evidence/run18/trigger.err (AttributeError), trigger_consumer.py vs trigger_consumer2.py.\n\nGATE ARM: Run `grep -n \"read()\" docs/ABSORB-TRIGGER.md`; expect that page to name the adapter method so a consumer following only it needs no source dive.","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-23T14:51:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-23T22:17:28Z","created_by":null,"source":null,"capability_tags":["docs"],"detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"76c4f0a8d08d945ddeac242a1d9b2c2413d0238f2fc3cfafb74099ef20fbd75d"},"branch":null,"worktree":null,"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"completed_at":null,"worker_status":"pending","foreman_note":null}
 {"id":"INFRA-LORE-046","status":"pending","priority":"P4","type":null,"title":"[P4] closes land without a task_completed event: LORE-20261012's two close commits touched tasks.jsonl only, so an events-derived close count undercounts","reasoning":"COS card-manager pass 2026-11-23T22:2xZ. LORE-20261012 closed at 15:32Z via commits 5d9eec8 and 07a42fa; both touched .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl and nothing else. events.jsonl's newest rows are the two task_created events (481, 482) for the dogfood rows, so the close has no audit event while its peers within the last eight closes all do. Second-order effect observed the same pass: the row's detail.evidence stayed null and its judge run dir .gitreins/history/2026-11-23/7425a512 was untracked, so the close read as unevidenced to every origin/main reader until this pass committed the run and bound --evidence-run-id. Not a duplicate of INFRA-LORE-045 (which covers a foreign evidence run being accepted).","acceptance_criteria":"The next lore row closed by lore-foreman appends a matching task_completed event to .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl in the same commit as the row, so the audit trail keeps one event per close.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-23 by the COS card manager: of the last eight closes on this board, seven carry a task_completed event (INFRA-LORE-045 event 474, LORE-EXPORT-1 event 468, RELEASE-LORE-010 event 473, LORE-072 event 476) while LORE-20261012 (closed 2026-11-23T15:32Z, commits 5d9eec8 + 07a42fa) carries none — its two close commits touched tasks.jsonl only. A reader that derives the day's closes from events undercounts by one, and the row's own evidence key was null until a later pass bound it.\n\nGATE ARM: Run `jq -r 'select(.task_id==\"LORE-20261012\")|.event_type' .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl` and `git log --name-only -1 --format=%H`; expect the next close commit to name BOTH tasks.jsonl and events.jsonl, and expect every close observed after this row to have a task_completed event with matching task_id.","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-23T22:21:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T22:28:17Z","created_by":null,"source":null,"capability_tags":[],"detail":{"fingerprint":"1766aa0c879dfccd1f25f019046071aaf0afdb04853921c946a107baf1be4d42"},"branch":null,"worktree":null,"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"completed_at":null,"worker_status":"pending","foreman_note":"COS measurement refining the cause, same pass: on this boardctl build  DOES emit an event (creating this row appended task_created event 483 at 22:21:06Z) while ,  and  emitted nothing — this pass's own three update calls (LORE-20261013 criteria, LORE-20261012 note+evidence-run-id, LORE-HYGIENE-20261122 note) produced no events, and the older closes that DO have events were written by a path that emitted them. So the defect is in the update/close event path of the writer, not a foreman forgetting a manual step.\n\nCORRECTION to the previous note (shell-mangled, disclosed): the preceding line lost four command tokens to backtick substitution before it was written. The intended measurement, re-stated plainly: on this boardctl build the create verb DOES emit an event (creating this row appended task_created event 483 at 2026-11-23T22:21:06Z) while the update verbs for status complete, note, and acceptance-criteria emitted nothing — this pass's own three update calls (LORE-20261013 criteria, LORE-20261012 note plus evidence-run-id, LORE-HYGIENE-20261122 note) produced no events, and the older closes that DO carry events were written by a path that emitted them. Conclusion unchanged: the defect sits in the update/close event path of the writer, not in a foreman forgetting a manual step.\n\nAC VERIFIED MET 2026-11-24T22:35Z (COS card manager, append-only). The next lore close after this row DID carry its event: QA-LORE-6 closed by commit 6b8b656, which names BOTH .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl and .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl (git show --stat 6b8b656: 2 files, 2 insertions, 1 deletion), and that commit's event is task_completed id 487, task_id QA-LORE-6, timestamp 2026-11-24T21:10:00Z, actor foreman, resolvable from origin/main. Both clauses of this row's GATE ARM therefore hold for the close path, so the defect as FILED (closes land without a task_completed event) did not reproduce.\n\nThis pass also re-measured the cause more precisely than the note above, and the writer split is not \"updates and closes emit nothing\" but per-verb: create emits (task_created 483 = this row, 484 = DOC-10-R2, 488-492 = the docs-audit batch), close-to-complete emits (487), and a plain update verb emits NOTHING — this pass's own boardctl update DOC-10-R2 --acceptance-criteria appended no event (DOC-10-R2's only event is still task_created 484, and events.jsonl stayed at 332 lines through the write). A reader deriving closes from events is therefore correct for this board, while a reader deriving NOTES or criteria repairs from events is not — that residual is the writer-plane question, and it is a narrower claim than this row's AC.\n\nDO NOT RE-DISPATCH this row for its filed AC. The owning lane closes it with its own run id and a commit hash; if the lane prefers to widen it to notes/criteria mutation events, that is a NEW row, not a reopen."}
